    "scene_specificity": {
      "total": 10,
      "specific_count": 10,
      "ratio": 1.0,
      "scenes": [
        {
          "id": "s01",
          "role": "hook",
          "est_duration_s": 9.7,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "glossary:swarm"
          ],
          "narration": "A swarm isn't many models. It's a single model taking turns. You already run that model in Ollama, and a swarm sounds like a pile of extra machines."
        },
        {
          "id": "s02",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 9.7,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "glossary:agent"
          ],
          "narration": "An agent is your Ollama chat with a name, a role, and tools. The same model answers as each agent. Every agent is that same model taking turns."
        },
        {
          "id": "s03",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 14.5,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:AutoGen"
          ],
          "narration": "So who speaks next? AutoGen's SelectorGroupChat hands that choice to a model. It reads the shared conversation and picks the next speaker. Each reply is broadcast to the whole team. A stop word or message cap, the termination condition, ends the run."
        },
        {
          "id": "s04",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 12.8,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:OpenAI",
            "entity:LangGraph"
          ],
          "narration": "OpenAI's Agents SDK does it with a tool call. A handoff, one agent passing the task, is a tool called transfer to refund agent. LangGraph instead shares one state, a common board every agent reads and writes."
        },
        {
          "id": "s05",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 15.2,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:localhost:11434"
          ],
          "narration": "Every framework points at a base U R L, the address for model requests. Set it to localhost, port eleven thousand four hundred thirty-four. One line re-points the swarm to your Ollama server. The client demands an A P I key; Ollama ignores it."
        },
        {
          "id": "s06",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 13.1,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "num:$2.00 / 1M tokens"
          ],
          "narration": "The deeper change is the bill. G P T six point one Sol charges two dollars per million input tokens, chunks of text. A swarm re-sends its conversation with every turn. Every message between agents pays that meter."
        },
        {
          "id": "s07",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 12.4,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "num:240 Watts",
            "entity:NVIDIA"
          ],
          "narration": "Your box never meters a token. NVIDIA's D G X Spark, built for this workload, ships with a two hundred forty watt power supply. Cloud charges per plate. Your box is a buffet, stove already on."
        },
        {
          "id": "s08",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 13.8,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "glossary:agent"
          ],
          "narration": "The buffet has a single stove, though. Ollama serves a single request at a time by default, and extra parallel slots cost memory. Your agents take turns. Want them at once? Then the myth has a point: parallelism costs memory."
        },
        {
          "id": "s09",
          "role": "explain",
          "est_duration_s": 7.6,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "entity:MAST"
          ],
          "narration": "The honest catch: MAST, the largest published audit of multi-agent failures. It annotated traces of real swarm runs across the popular frameworks."
        },
        {
          "id": "s10",
          "role": "payoff_close",
          "est_duration_s": 8.6,
          "specific": true,
          "hits": [
            "glossary:swarm",
            "glossary:token"
          ],
          "narration": "It sorted them into fourteen failure modes, mostly coordination, not weak models. So a local swarm buys you unlimited cheap tokens, not unlimited good ones."
        }
      ]
    },
